WEBVTT

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.800
First day of school! Wake up!
Come on. First day of school.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.240
I don't want to go to school.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.120
-Not you, Dad. Me.
-Okay.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.200
Get up! Time for school!

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.800
-All right, I'm up. It's time for school.
-Oh, boy!

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:38.960
Nemo!

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.800
-First day of school!
-Don't move.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.440
You'll never get out of there yourself.
I'll do it.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.360
-You feel a break?
-No.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.640
Sometimes fluid is rushing to the area.
Any rushing fluids?

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.440
-No.
-How many stripes do I have?

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.400
-Answer the question.
-Three.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.880
No! Something's wrong with you.
I have one, two...

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.840
Three. That's all I have?

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.920
You're okay. How's the lucky fin?

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.240
-Lucky.
-Let's see.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.160
Sure you want to go to school this year?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.960
-You can wait five or six years.
-Come on, Dad. It's time for school.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.320
-Forgot to brush.
-(SIGHS)

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.840
Do you want this anemone to sting you?

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.360
-Yes.
-Brush.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.960
-I'm done.
-You missed a spot.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.880
-Where?
-There.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.400
Right there. And here and here.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.600
We're excited. First day of school.
Here we go. We're ready to learn.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.880
What do we have to remember
about the ocean?

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.480
-It's not safe.
-That's my boy.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.360
First, we check to see that the coast
is clear. We go out and back in.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.680
Then we go out and back in.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.680
Then one more time. Out and back in.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.400
-If you want to do it four times...
-Dad...

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.440
All right. Come on, boy.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.720
Maybe while I'm at school,
I'll see a shark.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.440
-I doubt that.
-Have you ever met a shark?

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.240
-No, and I don't plan to.
-How old are sea turtles?

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.520
Sea turtles? I don't know.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.040
Sandy Plankton from next door said that

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.240
sea turtles live to be
about 100 years old.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.920
If I ever meet a sea turtle, I'll ask him,
after I'm done talking to the shark.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Hold on. Wait to cross.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.640
Hold my fin. Hold my fin.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.960
You're not going to freak out
like you did at the petting zoo.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.600
That snail was about to charge.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.520
I wonder where we're supposed to go.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.720
-Bye, Mom.
-I'll pick you up after school.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.520
Come on, you guys.
Stop it. Give it back.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.640
Come on. We'll try over there.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.600
Excuse me.
Is this where we meet his teacher?

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.240
-Look who's out of the anemone.
-Yes, shocking, I know.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.640
-Marty?
-Marlin.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:01.760
-Bob.
-Ted.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.840
Phil. Hey, you're a clownfish.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.680
You're funny, right? Tell us a joke.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.080
-Yeah.
-Good idea.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.320
That's a misconception. Clownfish are
no funnier than any other fish.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.880
-Come on, Clowny.
-Do something funny.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.200
All right. I know one joke.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.360
There's a mollusk. He walks up to...

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.160
Well, he swims up.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.080
Actually, the mollusk isn't moving.
He's in one place.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.560
And then the sea cucumber...

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.840
I'm mixed up. There was
a mollusk and a sea cucumber.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.800
None of them were walking...

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.040
Sheldon!
Get out of Mr. Johanssen's yard now!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.120
All right, you kids!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.200
Where'd you go? Where'd you go?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.680
Can I go play, too? Can I?

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.520
I would feel better if you go play
over on the sponge beds.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.000
-(MOTHER GASPS)
-(BABY CRIES)

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.960
That's where I would play.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.040
-What's wrong with his fin?
-He looks funny.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.640
-Hey, what did I do?
-Be nice. It's his first time at school.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.200
He was born with it.
We call it his lucky fin.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.360
Dad...

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:12.200
See this tentacle?
It's shorter than all my other tentacles.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.640
But you can't really tell.
Especially when I twirl them like this.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.680
I'm H2O intolerant.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.240
I'm obnoxious.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.200
♪ Let's name the zones,
the zones, the zones

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.040
♪ Let's name the zones of the open sea

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.400
Mr. Ray!

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.520
-Come on, Nemo.
-Stay with me.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.480
♪ There's epipelagic, mesopelagic,
bathyal, abyssopelagic

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.040
♪ All the rest are too deep
for you and me to see

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.800
I wonder where my class has gone.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.720
We're under here.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.520
There you are! Come aboard, explorers.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.120
♪ Knowledge exploring is oh so lyrical

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.640
♪ When you think thoughts
that are empirical ♪

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.040
Dad, you can go now.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.080
-Well, hello. Who is this?
-I'm Nemo.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.640
Nemo, all new explorers
must answer a science question.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.640
-Okay.
-You live in what kind of home?

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.920
In an anemoninny.
Anemonemenemone.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.400
Don't hurt yourself. Welcome aboard.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.480
Just so you know, he's got a little fin.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.080
If he's having trouble swimming,
let him take a break. 15 minutes.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.320
Dad, it's time for you to go now.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.560
We're going to stay together.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.240
Okay, class. Optical orbits up front.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.680
Remember, we keep our
supraesophageal ganglion to ourselves.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.520
-That means you, Jimmy.
-Oh, man!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.960
-Bye, Nemo.
-Bye, Dad.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.680
Bye, son.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.080
Be safe.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.520
You're doing well for a first-timer.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.920
You can't hold on to them forever,
can you?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.160
I had a tough time when
my eldest went out on the Drop Off.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.800
The Drop Off!
They're going to the Drop Off?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.480
Are you insane?

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.440
Why don't we fry them up now
and serve them with chips?

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.160
Hey, Marty, calm down.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.040
Don't tell me to be calm, pony-boy.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.800
Pony-boy?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.640
For a clownfish,
he really isn't that funny.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.760
Pity.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.280
♪ Let's name the species,
the species, the species

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.200
♪ Let's name the species
that live in the sea

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.880
♪ Mollusca and gastropoda, arthropoda,
echinoderma, chordata

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.280
♪ And some fish like you and me!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.240
Come on. Sing with me.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.920
♪ Seaweed is cool, seaweed is fun

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.040
♪ It makes its food
from the rays of the sun ♪

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.840
Okay, the Drop Off.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.160
All right, kids.
Feel free to explore, but stay close.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.960
Stromatolitic cyanobacteria! Gather.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.280
An ecosystem contained
in one infinitesimal speck.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.320
(RAMBLES ON)

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.360
Come on. Let's go.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.360
Come on. Sing with me.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.400
♪ There's porifera, coelenterata,
hydrozoa, scyphozoa

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.120
♪ Anthozoa, ctenophora,
bryozoas three ♪

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.840
Hey, guys, wait up.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.240
Whoa!

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.400
Cool.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.160
Saved your life!

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.720
-You guys made me ink.
-(LAUGHTER)

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.960
What's that?

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.440
I know what that is.
Sandy Plankton saw one.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.640
He said it was called a butt.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.360
Wow. That's a pretty big butt.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.440
Look at me.
I'm going to go touch the butt.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.440
(LAUGHTER)

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.400
Oh, yeah? Let's see you get closer.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.720
Okay.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.560
Beat that.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.160
Come on, Nemo. How far can you go?

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.560
-My dad says it's not safe.
-Nemo, no!

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.760
Dad?

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.440
You were about to
swim into open water.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.560
No!

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.400
Good thing I was here.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.920
-He wasn't going to go.
-He was too afraid.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.600
-I wasn't.
-This does not concern you.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:09.080
You're lucky I don't tell your parents.
You can't swim well.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.440
-I can swim fine, Dad, okay?
-No. It's not okay.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.960
You shouldn't be near here.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.600
You'll start school in a year or two.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.760
No. Just because
you're scared of the ocean...

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.760
Clearly you're not ready.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.840
You think you can do these things,
but you just can't!

